<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument · artifact</p><h1 class="enc-title">Skype</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/2003">2003</a>–2025</span> · <a href="/centuries/21st-century">21st century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Skype was an internet telephony and video-calling service launched in 2003 by Niklas Zennström and Janus Friis, whose software was written by the Estonian developers Ahti Heinla, Priit Kasesalu and Jaan Tallinn. It became one of the most widely used communication services in the world and a symbol of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estonia">Estonia</a>'s technology sector. It was bought by eBay in 2005 and Microsoft in 2011, which closed it in 2025.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/skype.jpg" alt="Skype" width="320" height="324" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Skype Technologies · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Skype_logo_(2019%E2%80%93present).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
